    cat: "Music & Sonic Culture", c: "lo-fi synth-pop microgenre", e: "community_subculture", o: "Washed Out's Ernest Greene, Toro y Moi and Memory Tapes, blog-named in 2009",
    g: "US Southeast (Georgia, South Carolina) and the music-blogosphere", p: "2009-2012", era: "late blog era",
    sum: "Sun-bleached synths and hissed vocals about remembered summers — the first genre made, named and killed by the blogosphere.",
    desc: "Chillwave arrived in mid-2009 when blogs — notably Hipster Runoff, which coined the name — and writers like Simon Reynolds (offering 'hypnagogic pop') tried to classify a wave of bedroom producers using hazy vintage synths, filtered vocals, drum-machine softshoes and VHS-warm nostalgia. Washed Out's 'Feel It All Around' (2009) became the sound's face as the Portlandia theme; Toro y Moi's Causers of This (2010) and Washed Out's Within and Without (2011) filled the small canon. Everything was lo-fi by design: tape hiss, detuned Junos, beach-poster color. Journalists declared the genre dead by 2012, but its methods seeded synth-pop revivalism, vaporwave's warmth and the lo-fi beats playlists of the streaming decade.",
    col: [{ h: "#e8b08a", n: "VHS peach" }, { h: "#5aa8a0", n: "pool teal" }, { h: "#e8cf7a", n: "sun haze yellow" }, { h: "#8aa0b2", n: "bleach denim" }, { h: "#a07a8a", n: "dusk mauve" }],
